 and 20x) of 0.1 M CeO and 0.1 M 20% Gd-CeO NPs (Fig. 12B, right panel). However, the H2O2-induced reduction in cell viability measured by MTT test was modestly, but significantly, attenuated by 20x dilution of 0.1 M CeO and 0.1 M 20% Gd-CeO NPs; for dilution 10x of both types of NPs, we observed only some tendency for neuroprotection (p < 0.12) (Fig. 12B, left panel). The assessment of LDH release and MTT reduction in the Glu model of neuronal cell damage revealed significant differences between groups, as assessed by the one-way ANOVA (F5,6 = 12.8, p = 0.004 and F5,6 = 23.6, p = 0.0000, respectively) (Fig. 12B). However, after post hoc analysis, we did not observe any protection mediated by both tested dilutions of 0.1 M CeO and 0.1 M 20% Gd-CeO NPs against neuronal cell damage induced by Glu, as verified by LDH release and MTT assays (Fig. 12C).
